    <section class="section about">
      <div class="container about-grid">
        <div class="about-copy">
          <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>Comfort Club</span>
          <h2>Protect Your Investment &amp; Avoid Unexpected Breakdowns</h2>
          <p class="lead">Your heating and air conditioning system is one of the biggest investments in your home. Just like changing the oil in your car, regular preventive maintenance extends the life of your equipment, preserves your manufacturer warranty, and keeps your monthly utility bills as low as possible.</p>
          <p class="lead" style="margin-top:14px">With a Mid Lakes HVAC service agreement, you never have to worry about remembering to schedule your seasonal tune-ups. Our team handles the maintenance for you, keeping your home comfortable in every season.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="faq-media">
          <img src="../images/wall-units.webp" alt="Ductless mini-split units mounted on the exterior wall of a home" />
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section services">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-title">
          <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>Included</span>
          <h2>What&rsquo;s Included in Your Maintenance Agreement</h2>
          <p class="lead">Our preventive service program is designed to give you total peace of mind and exclusive financial savings throughout the year:</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="service-grid">
          <li class="service-card">
            <h3>Two Annual Tune-Ups</h3>
            <p>Comprehensive seasonal maintenance, one Spring AC tune-up and one Fall Heating tune-up, to prepare your system for extreme Georgia weather.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="service-card">
            <h3>Priority 24/7 Dispatch</h3>
            <p>Program members receive priority scheduling on all service calls, including late-night and weekend emergencies.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="service-card">
            <h3>Exclusive Repair Discounts</h3>
            <p>Enjoy special member pricing and discounts on all needed parts and labor.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="service-card">
            <h3>Lower Monthly Energy Bills</h3>
            <p>Properly cleaned and calibrated systems run at peak efficiency, helping slash monthly power costs.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="service-card">
            <h3>Extended Equipment Lifespan</h3>
            <p>Regular tune-ups catch minor wear-and-tear before it turns into a major, expensive system breakdown.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="service-card">
            <h3>Warranty Protection</h3>
            <p>Most HVAC manufacturers require proof of annual professional maintenance to keep valid warranty coverage on parts.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section about">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-title">
          <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>Inspections</span>
          <h2>What Happens During Your Annual Inspections?</h2>
          <p class="lead">Our certified technicians bring over 75 years of combined experience to every tune-up.</p>
          <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">Here is a look at our comprehensive inspection process:</p>
        </div>
        <div class="group-grid">
          <div class="spec-card spec-card--blue">
            <p class="spec-label">Spring Air Conditioning Tune-Up</p>
            <ul class="spec-list">
              <li>Inspect and clean evaporator &amp; condenser coils</li>
              <li>Check refrigerant charge levels &amp; system pressure</li>
              <li>Inspect &amp; flush condensate drain lines to prevent water damage</li>
              <li>Test capacitors, relays, &amp; electrical connections</li>
              <li>Calibrate thermostat &amp; verify proper airflow</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-card">
            <p class="spec-label">Fall Heating System Tune-Up</p>
            <ul class="spec-list">
              <li>Inspect heat exchanger &amp; burner assembly</li>
              <li>Test safety controls &amp; ignition systems</li>
              <li>Inspect blower motor &amp; check system components</li>
              <li>Check gas line connections &amp; vent piping</li>
              <li>Replace or inspect standard air filters</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section faq" id="faq">
      <div class="container faq-grid">
        <div class="faq-list-wrap">
          <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>FAQs</span>
          <h2>Maintenance Program FAQs</h2>
          <div class="faq-list">
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>Do maintenance plans cover ductless mini-split systems as well as central HVAC?<span class="faq-mark"></span></summary>
              <p>Yes. We provide expert preventive maintenance for both central heating and air systems as well as ductless mini-split units. Call our Loganville office at (678) 776-0591 to discuss coverage for your home&rsquo;s setup.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>Why is preventive HVAC maintenance required for my manufacturer warranty?<span class="faq-mark"></span></summary>
              <p>Most major HVAC brands (including Rheem&reg;) require annual professional tune-ups to keep warranty coverage valid. Regular servicing provides documented proof of care if you ever need a covered parts replacement.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>Can I join the Maintenance Program if my system is older or installed by another company?<span class="faq-mark"></span></summary>
              <p>Yes. Our technicians bring over 75 years of combined experience servicing all major brands and equipment ages across Loganville and surrounding areas.</p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="faq-media">
          <img src="../images/vents.webp" alt="Modern rooftop ventilation vents on a concrete facade" />
          <figcaption><strong>Two visits a year.</strong> One Spring AC tune-up and one Fall heating tune-up, scheduled for you.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

